{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
  "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Elena Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Article I of the Constitution permits Congress to enact section 4248, which is the limited Federal civil commitment statute at issue in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, is part of the statutory scheme that you can be committed to Federal custody for, say, a year and then the State takes it over?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What -- what -- what power conferred upon the Federal Government by the Constitution permits the Federal Government to assure that sexual predators are not at large?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Elena Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that that's not right, Justice Scalia. I think that there is a transition period, and what this statute is designed to do is to deal with that transition period and to make sure that sexually dangerous, mentally ill people don't fall through the cracks between Federal custody and the reestablishment of State control."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General Elena Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, if you go back to a case like Kansas v. Hendricks, which is of course where this Court thought about civil commitment statutes with relation to sexually dangerous offenders, I think the Court made clear that it was important in that case that there be not only sexual dangerousness, but also mental illness, in order to invoke the civil commitment statutes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What about release from the Army? Would that -- would that also -- if I want to turn this -- this person after discharge at -- you know, loose upon the society, could the Federal Government commit that person?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "G. Alan DuBois",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I really think the government gives the game away a bit in its opening statement when it characterized this law as a law that was necessary to prevent the problem of releasing sexually dangerous individuals. And I don't think that that is what the Necessary and Proper Clause is designed to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And so what's the power that the Federal Government is exercising when it commits someone who has been found not guilty by reason of insanity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "G. Alan DuBois",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would say that, in the same way that mental health is a uniquely State function, so too is public health. And we would say that, no, the Federal Government cannot detain that person past the end of his sentence, and that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "G. Alan DuBois",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, Justice Breyer, I don't think the Federal Government has that power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: The government has some responsibility, doesn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dubois",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DUBOIS: And it seems to me that the government's argument essentially collapses into the notion, well, if it's a good idea, it must be necessary and proper to do it. I think that\u2019s just simply not correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dubois",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DUBOIS: Right. And -- and -- well, I think there\u2019s -- there\u2019s a number of weapons in the Federal Government's arsenal. First of all, there\u2019s the Federal spending power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8073d5c66b75b4a7c0d3748910c862bbba06db37b9dd1e7674446ef60ce78d7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8073d5c66b75-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But that doesn't take care of the fact that the prisoner would be released before there was a cure found for the alleged mental illness, meaning supervised release generally has a term limit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1224",
      "confidence": 0.0,
